    Napoleon: *Sighs* This can have more than one reason, you know.
    Napoleon: I had to search his pocket once because I knew without a doubt that my newly disapeard ring would be just there waiting for me.
    Napoleon: He tried to resist. Random circus visitors were wathing. That was a humilating sigh.
    Napoleon: *Pauses* For him.
        -> You: What happened next?
            Napoleon: I found the ring, of course. And a considerable amount of cookie cramps. *Looks disgusted*
        -> You: What if it wasnt in his pockets?
            Napoleon: Oh I would have left the scene.. as fast as I could...
            Napoleon: ... To check his wagon.
            Napoleon: Anyway. I found the ring, And a considerable amount of cookie cramps. *Looks disgusted*
        Napoleon: Told him next time this happens I'll break his leg...
        <<wait  1>>
        Napoleon: Ah, dont give me that detective look. I woulnt have gone farer than getting a leg.
        Napoleon: He didny need a leg to play his trumpet.
        You: Understandable.
    Napoleon: Anyhow... *leans back in his chair* What had the old crow stuffed in his nest?
    -> You: I have found many belongings of Ms. Mort in the crime scene. 
        <<jump Nap_Mort>>

